Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.74,0:00:42.48,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,For Noriyaki Kakyoin,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.80,0:00:46.74,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Hierophant Green served as a poignant\Nreminder of a time long past.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.42,0:00:50.54,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,It's Noriaki.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.76,0:00:53.54,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,He doesn't attempt to socialize\Nwith the other children.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.62,0:00:57.68,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,It's not that he's disliked per se;\Nhe just seems a bit too reserved.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.40,0:01:00.76,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,As his teacher, I'm very concerned.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.38,0:01:05.68,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I'm ashamed to say it, but I'm\Nafraid I don't understand it either.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.06,0:01:09.30,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I always had the same thoughts.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.74,0:01:14.45,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Life is full of interactions\Nwhere we meet all sorts of people.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.56,0:01:17.74,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,But how often do those meetings\Ninvolve deeper thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.82,0:01:20.59,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,How often do we make\Ngenuine human connections?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.38,0:01:26.67,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,All of my classmates have address\Nbooks filled with their friends' names.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.14,0:01:29.26,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Each of them must have a book of 50.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.46,0:01:30.92,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,No, a hundred names.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.84,0:01:34.64,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Mom has Dad, and Dad has Mom.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.84,0:01:35.90,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,But I have no one.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.06,0:01:40.20,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I'm sure rock stars and TV celebrities\Nhave tens of thousands of friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.28,0:01:41.66,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,But I have no one.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.14,0:01:43.79,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I'll never have any friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.40,0:01:46.22,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,No one will ever understand me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.18,0:01:49.89,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I'm the only one who can\Nsee Hierophant Green.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.44,0:01:54.85,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,How am I supposed to truly relate to\Nsomeone if they can't see the real me?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.00,0:01:56.00,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,It's impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.30,0:02:00.42,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,That's how I used to think\Nabout life, until I met Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.50,0:02:03.92,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Joestar, Jotaro, Polnareff, and Avdol.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.72,0:02:07.96,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Whenever I think about Avdol and Iggy,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.04,0:02:11.28,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,it makes the hairs on the\Nback of my neck stand on end.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.48,0:02:15.48,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I'm sure it's because they were the\Nfirst to treat me like a friend.
